+### `--openssl-ca-bundled-fallback`
+
+<!-- YAML
+added: REPLACEME
+-->
+
+In builds configured with `--openssl-use-def-ca-store`, Node.js uses OpenSSL's
+default CA store. With this option, which is the default in such builds, the
+bundled Mozilla CA store is added when OpenSSL has no CA location configured:
+neither `SSL_CERT_FILE` nor `SSL_CERT_DIR` is set and nothing exists at
+OpenSSL's default certificate file or directory. A configured location is
+used as is, even when it is empty. An explicit `--use-openssl-ca` disables
+this behavior, as does `--no-openssl-ca-bundled-fallback`.
+
